# Lint debt, ratcheted. This number may go DOWN, never up.
#
# The limits in `clippy.toml` were adopted whole (T85) against a tree that
# predates them, so 290 sites tripped at once. Denying outright would stop the
# tree compiling and block every other task; a blanket `allow` is the reflex
# the limits exist to catch. So the lints WARN, this file records the count,
# and the gate fails when the count RISES.
#
# The check that can fail is this comparison, not clippy -- which is what
# keeps `.:B6` satisfied: a check that cannot fail is no check.
#
# When a lint's own debt reaches zero, flip it from `warn` to `deny` in
# Cargo.toml individually and it stops needing this file.
#
# GROUPS, measured 2026-08-19:
#   structural  ~69  (fell 14 when T17 decomposed the titrations)   too_many_lines, cognitive_complexity, excessive_nesting,
#                    too_many_arguments -- the decomposition signal (.:V109)
#   safety     198   indexing_slicing, arithmetic_side_effects, unwrap, expect
#
# Lowering this belongs to `.:T92` (split src/tdd) and the pay-down tasks, and
# a drop should arrive WITH the refactor that earned it.
#
# RAISED 270 -> 271 on 2026-08-23, deliberately, and this is the reason the
# rule asks for.
#
# `fed::nav` is 18 lines against a 15-line limit: it walks the path from root
# to a node and emits one row per step, with the step that reaches the node
# emitting `self` plus every sibling. Splitting the step out produced
# `nav_step(root, node, parent, cur, name)` -- five parameters against a
# four-parameter limit, so the split traded one warning for another AND made
# the function harder to read, since every value the loop already had has to
# be threaded back in.
#
# That is the limit misfiring on a walk rather than catching complexity, and
# `clippy.toml`'s own header says these thresholds are the shape the target
# model handles, not a law. A raise recorded with its cause is what this file
# is for; a contortion that satisfies the counter and worsens the code is
# what `.:B6` warns against.
#
# It comes back down with `.:T92`.
total 271
